From a1d52b465aa8bb793e706f482f262caeccc12431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:31:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] nvk/rm: execution and bind contexts

Exec contexts follow NVIDIA's own channel setup (nvidia-push-init.c and
nv_gpu_ops.c in open-gpu-kernel-modules):

  KEPLER_CHANNEL_GROUP_A (GR engine, our VA space) under the device
    FERMI_CONTEXT_SHARE_A (async subcontext)
    the GPU's GPFIFO class (BLACKWELL_CHANNEL_GPFIFO_B on GB20x) with a
    client-allocated 1024-entry ring, USERD and error notifier
      3D, compute and copy objects as requested (no parameters; RM
      allocates the GR context buffers in the VA space's internal range)
  SET_WORK_SUBMIT_TOKEN_NOTIF_INDEX + GET_WORK_SUBMIT_TOKEN, then
  NVA06C_CTRL_CMD_GPFIFO_SCHEDULE on the TSG.

The GPFIFO ring and per-entry push slots are our own system pages; the
error notifier and USERD are RM-allocated system memory, since RM writes
the notifier itself.

Submission needs no RM call: exec() writes GPFIFO entries (NO_PREFETCH
becomes SYNC_WAIT, an incomplete push is simply followed by the next
entry), flush() publishes GP_PUT in USERD and writes the work-submit
token to the usermode doorbell.  A full ring waits for GP_GET.  Channel
errors reported in the error notifier turn into VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST.

sync() releases a context-private 64-bit semaphore with WFI from the
pushbuffer, raises a non-stall interrupt and waits for the value on the
CPU: a short spin, then poll() on the non-stall OS event when librmclient
provides one (only as a wakeup, the value in memory decides), else
sleeping with backoff.

Bind contexts have no RM queue: binds are applied synchronously with
NV_ESC_RM_MAP/UNMAP_MEMORY_DMA.

Waiting on and signaling vk_syncs is not wired up yet.

